          "page": 5,
          "section": "2. Experimental",
          "quote": "The laser system used for the experiments is the 6 kW IPG Ytterbium laser System 6000. The additive materials were delivered using discrete coaxial blown powder jets. Argon carrier gas at flow rate of 4 𝑙/min at the pressure of 0.2 MPa was used for the coaxial powder delivery. In addition, argon shielding gas at flow rate of 20 l/min and pressure of 0.1 MPa was used at the base of the nozzle to protect the laser optics and to minimize melt-pool oxidation. Based on a series of printing parameter optimizations, the utilized laser process parameters were laser power of 880 W, with a beam size of 2.5 mm, laser scanning velocity of 10 mm/s, and powder feeding rate of 8.6 g/min.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
